1
00:01:24,126 --> 00:01:24,960
Special Forces!

2
00:01:28,172 --> 00:01:29,215
Are you okay?

3
00:01:31,467 --> 00:01:34,261
Sir, are you okay?

4
00:01:34,345 --> 00:01:36,472
You're more injured than I am.

5
00:01:39,934 --> 00:01:41,060
Hold still.

6
00:01:41,143 --> 00:01:42,937
My gosh, Secretary Kang!

7
00:01:43,020 --> 00:01:44,313
My goodness.

8
00:01:44,814 --> 00:01:46,440
What on earth just happened?

9
00:01:46,524 --> 00:01:48,025
The chandelier…

10
00:01:48,818 --> 00:01:50,694
How about you? Are you okay, Mr. Yoon?

11
00:01:50,778 --> 00:01:52,988
-Bring the first aid kit.
-Yes, sir.

12
00:01:53,072 --> 00:01:54,657
First aid kit!

13
00:01:54,740 --> 00:01:55,783
Hello, Director?

14
00:01:56,575 --> 00:01:58,244
We need to go to your hospital.

15
00:01:58,327 --> 00:01:59,745
It's not that serious.

16
00:02:01,455 --> 00:02:02,581
You're clearly in pain.

17
00:02:03,874 --> 00:02:05,459
We'll be there in ten minutes.

18
00:02:05,543 --> 00:02:07,920
My secretary got severely injured and--

19
00:02:09,088 --> 00:02:11,131
I'm okay. There's nothing wrong with me.

20
00:02:13,384 --> 00:02:14,927
What are you doing?

21
00:02:15,010 --> 00:02:17,638
I'm really fine.
I didn't fracture any bones.

22
00:02:19,098 --> 00:02:20,808
Here's the first aid kit.

23
00:02:21,767 --> 00:02:22,977
This will do.

24
00:02:23,644 --> 00:02:24,728
What do you--

25
00:02:26,814 --> 00:02:28,232
Special Forces!

26
00:02:29,567 --> 00:02:30,484
Oh my.

27
00:03:02,975 --> 00:03:06,395
Can such a big chandelier
just fall off like that?

28
00:03:06,478 --> 00:03:09,189
It's gotten dimmer
than how it was when I left yesterday.

29
00:03:09,273 --> 00:03:11,567
So you can see those details.

30
00:03:11,650 --> 00:03:14,820
From now on,
you need to protect me even more.

31
00:03:14,904 --> 00:03:18,282
That's how it felt
when I lifted the bottle.

32
00:03:18,365 --> 00:03:21,076
Something must've been added to the milk.

33
00:03:21,160 --> 00:03:25,581
You'll soon realize
how dangerous a place you've stepped into.

34
00:03:33,756 --> 00:03:36,300
Why won't you go and see a doctor?

35
00:03:40,679 --> 00:03:41,680
Open the door.

36
00:03:42,848 --> 00:03:43,933
Open it.

37
00:03:44,016 --> 00:03:44,975
Open the door!

38
00:03:45,059 --> 00:03:45,976
What is it?

39
00:03:46,060 --> 00:03:47,895
Open the door now!

40
00:03:47,978 --> 00:03:49,396
I'm not seriously injured.

41
00:03:49,480 --> 00:03:51,649
-Damn it.
-You better open the door now!

42
00:03:51,732 --> 00:03:53,984
But is that really something
to get so angry about?

43
00:03:58,405 --> 00:03:59,990
Mom, open the door.

44
00:04:00,532 --> 00:04:02,034
Open the door.

45
00:04:06,080 --> 00:04:07,164
Mom.

46
00:04:07,957 --> 00:04:09,249
Come on, open the door.

47
00:04:21,261 --> 00:04:22,096
Mom?

48
00:04:28,644 --> 00:04:30,437
Can you just wait?

49
00:04:31,855 --> 00:04:32,982
Bring the key!

50
00:04:33,857 --> 00:04:34,692
Yes, sir.

51
00:04:37,194 --> 00:04:39,238
Sir, here's the key.

52
00:04:43,117 --> 00:04:44,451
Are you okay, Special Forces?

53
00:05:06,682 --> 00:05:08,183
You shouldn't be worried about me.

54
00:05:09,393 --> 00:05:12,980
If I hadn't pushed you out of the way,
you'd be dead at worst.

55
00:05:14,148 --> 00:05:15,607
You told me to be on my toes.

56
00:05:15,691 --> 00:05:18,152
You said I'd see
how dangerous a place I'd stepped into.

57
00:05:18,235 --> 00:05:20,988
Is this what you meant
when you said all that?

58
00:05:21,488 --> 00:05:22,906
Are you really being shy?

59
00:05:23,991 --> 00:05:25,826
At least button up properly.

60
00:05:27,828 --> 00:05:29,621
I just have a scratch on my arm. Look.

61
00:05:31,415 --> 00:05:33,125
Who goes to the hospital over this?

62
00:05:35,502 --> 00:05:36,795
Earlier,

63
00:05:38,005 --> 00:05:40,716
I said something was happening here
that I don't know about.

64
00:05:41,925 --> 00:05:45,429
What is it that only you know
but I don't, Mr. Yoon?

65
00:06:12,748 --> 00:06:13,624
Don't be a baby.

66
00:06:15,876 --> 00:06:18,921
You weren't in the special forces,
were you?

67
00:06:19,004 --> 00:06:20,506
You've seen what I can do.

68
00:06:21,548 --> 00:06:23,008
I saved your life.

69
00:06:25,844 --> 00:06:27,721
Are you not going to answer me?

70
00:06:31,934 --> 00:06:32,893
No.

71
00:06:34,353 --> 00:06:35,395
I won't.

72
00:06:39,108 --> 00:06:40,442
Because you don't need to?

73
00:06:41,860 --> 00:06:43,529
You fired me, so I should get lost?

74
00:06:47,950 --> 00:06:49,034
Stay still.

75
00:06:59,795 --> 00:07:02,673
What happened? Are you okay?

76
00:07:02,756 --> 00:07:03,590
Are you hurt?

77
00:07:03,674 --> 00:07:05,551
Secretary Kang! What happened?

78
00:07:05,634 --> 00:07:08,637
What on earth is going on here?

79
00:07:08,720 --> 00:07:12,474
There's blood everywhere!
What just happened?

80
00:07:12,558 --> 00:07:14,101
You have to go see a doctor!

81
00:07:14,184 --> 00:07:15,644
What about the chandelier?

82
00:07:15,727 --> 00:07:17,396
Tell me what happened.

83
00:07:17,479 --> 00:07:19,189
That chandelier didn't fall on its own.

84
00:07:20,649 --> 00:07:22,317
No wonder you were acting strange.

85
00:07:22,401 --> 00:07:23,777
Is that why you hired Mr. Kang?

86
00:07:26,196 --> 00:07:28,448
I knew you'd be attacked over the company,

87
00:07:28,532 --> 00:07:30,200
but this crossed the line.

88
00:07:30,284 --> 00:07:31,827
Why not tell the chairman?

89
00:07:32,327 --> 00:07:35,455
He might've expected this,
or he might already know.

90
00:07:37,624 --> 00:07:38,792
How scary.

91
00:07:38,876 --> 00:07:40,252
He knew and stayed silent?

92
00:07:40,335 --> 00:07:43,213
I'm not the only one
aware of how he operates.

93
00:07:43,297 --> 00:07:44,715
We saw him while growing up.

94
00:07:45,841 --> 00:07:48,594
"No need to play fair.
Do whatever it takes to win."

95
00:07:48,677 --> 00:07:50,012
"And you have my approval."

96
00:07:50,095 --> 00:07:51,263
Who do you think did this?

97
00:07:54,099 --> 00:07:55,058
Can you guess?

98
00:07:59,980 --> 00:08:00,939
Are you injured?

99
00:08:01,440 --> 00:08:02,274
I'm fine, sir.

100
00:08:04,276 --> 00:08:05,569
Park Min-hwan disappeared.

101
00:08:05,652 --> 00:08:06,612
But

102
00:08:07,571 --> 00:08:09,698
someone else is also tracking him down.

103
00:08:10,741 --> 00:08:11,658
What?

104
00:08:11,742 --> 00:08:13,368
The chandelier that fell.

105
00:08:13,452 --> 00:08:15,537
I don't think it fell on its own.

106
00:08:16,079 --> 00:08:17,789
Yoon Yi-jun seemed to have expected it.

107
00:08:17,873 --> 00:08:18,957
What's going on?

108
00:08:19,499 --> 00:08:22,252
Everything that goes around here is off.

109
00:08:25,756 --> 00:08:28,050
I don't think
there's anyone better than him.

110
00:08:30,177 --> 00:08:31,094
So tell me.

111
00:08:31,178 --> 00:08:33,013
Tell you what?

112
00:08:33,096 --> 00:08:34,848
How to rescind firing someone

113
00:08:34,932 --> 00:08:36,391
without losing face?

114
00:08:36,475 --> 00:08:38,310
Like if it violated
the Labor Standards Act

115
00:08:38,393 --> 00:08:40,854
or was otherwise unlawful
and therefore invalid.

116
00:08:40,938 --> 00:08:42,481
It's usually 30 days.

117
00:08:42,564 --> 00:08:45,692
That's the legal notice period
for dismissal.

118
00:08:45,776 --> 00:08:48,570
Since I gave the notice today,
I violated the labor laws, right?

119
00:08:48,654 --> 00:08:49,529
So I can't fire him.

120
00:08:49,613 --> 00:08:51,281
Look at that smile on your face.

121
00:08:51,365 --> 00:08:52,908
But that doesn't apply to Mr. Kang.

122
00:08:52,991 --> 00:08:54,576
Not with the contract we signed.

123
00:08:54,660 --> 00:08:55,827
You drew up the contract.

124
00:08:55,911 --> 00:08:57,287
You authorized it.

125
00:08:59,998 --> 00:09:02,209
Whatever. Find a way.

126
00:09:19,393 --> 00:09:20,352
I'm leaving.

127
00:09:23,105 --> 00:09:24,022
Secretary Kang.

128
00:09:25,565 --> 00:09:28,944
You should still see a doctor,
just in case.

129
00:09:29,027 --> 00:09:32,364
You won't be able to get compensation
if you get treated too late.

130
00:09:32,447 --> 00:09:34,533
If that's the case,
I won't press charges later.

131
00:09:35,492 --> 00:09:37,703
Well, if you insist.

132
00:09:43,000 --> 00:09:46,920
Just call me anytime
if you want compensation.

133
00:09:47,004 --> 00:09:49,298
You just saved a billionaire heir's life.

134
00:09:49,381 --> 00:09:51,091
I'll squeeze out max compensation.

135
00:09:52,467 --> 00:09:54,720
-Oh my.
-You said you'd leave.

136
00:09:54,803 --> 00:09:56,471
-Right.
-Aren't you going to leave?

137
00:09:56,555 --> 00:09:59,057
-Leave.
-Wait, the door is that way.

138
00:10:03,603 --> 00:10:05,772
Employers aren't allowed to
dismiss employees

139
00:10:05,856 --> 00:10:07,607
when they're getting medical treatment.

140
00:10:08,191 --> 00:10:10,694
So under Article 23, Clause 2
of the Labor Standards Act,

141
00:10:10,777 --> 00:10:13,155
you can't fire him.

142
00:10:14,072 --> 00:10:15,032
Did I do well?

143
00:10:16,491 --> 00:10:18,368
-Leave.
-What?

144
00:10:18,452 --> 00:10:19,328
Go.

145
00:10:20,662 --> 00:10:22,080
You said you have plans.

146
00:10:23,248 --> 00:10:24,958
Do I?

147
00:10:25,042 --> 00:10:27,169
-Hold on, Attorney Kim.
-What?

148
00:10:28,879 --> 00:10:30,380
-Really?
-Really what?

149
00:10:30,464 --> 00:10:31,590
I'm not getting fired?

150
00:10:32,174 --> 00:10:33,133
No.

151
00:10:33,842 --> 00:10:34,760
Goodbye.

152
00:10:35,469 --> 00:10:38,680
It seems I'm more injured
than I thought, sir.

153
00:10:38,764 --> 00:10:40,599
I'll bring you a medical note.

154
00:10:41,516 --> 00:10:42,642
Follow me.

155
00:10:52,611 --> 00:10:54,154
Do you know

156
00:10:55,155 --> 00:10:57,491
how hard it is to follow a crisis protocol

157
00:10:58,075 --> 00:10:59,534
in an urgent situation?

158
00:11:00,118 --> 00:11:02,871
Without my quick thinking, sound judgment,

159
00:11:02,954 --> 00:11:04,706
and calmness under pressure,

160
00:11:04,790 --> 00:11:08,168
it would've been much harder
to save you, sir.

161
00:11:12,255 --> 00:11:15,509
Are you saying you were able
to pull it off, Special Forces?

162
00:11:16,343 --> 00:11:17,260
Yes, sir!

163
00:11:17,344 --> 00:11:18,845
And you want me to acknowledge it?

164
00:11:18,929 --> 00:11:20,013
Yes, sir.

165
00:11:20,097 --> 00:11:21,264
But that's your job.

166
00:11:21,973 --> 00:11:23,308
Who are you trying to fool?

167
00:11:23,850 --> 00:11:24,893
You're right, sir.

168
00:11:26,520 --> 00:11:27,729
Be honest.

169
00:11:29,689 --> 00:11:30,732
You saw everything

170
00:11:32,275 --> 00:11:33,527
in the last room upstairs.

171
00:11:39,658 --> 00:11:40,784
Found it.

172
00:11:43,286 --> 00:11:45,580
NO MESSAGES

173
00:11:45,664 --> 00:11:46,581
What?

174
00:11:50,710 --> 00:11:51,920
What?

175
00:11:55,590 --> 00:11:57,509
It doesn't seem to be
Han Eun-young's phone.

176
00:11:58,135 --> 00:11:59,636
Is it the same model?

177
00:12:29,458 --> 00:12:31,251
Well, I just

178
00:12:31,334 --> 00:12:34,129
took a quick look inside. That's all.

179
00:12:35,422 --> 00:12:36,256
You saw it.

180
00:12:40,469 --> 00:12:42,721
I knew this would happen.

181
00:12:46,141 --> 00:12:47,434
After seeing all that,

182
00:12:49,019 --> 00:12:51,438
where did you think
you were going to run off to?

183
00:12:51,521 --> 00:12:52,814
I wasn't running off.

184
00:12:52,898 --> 00:12:57,944
I'm dying to hear
what rumors you would've spread about me.

185
00:12:58,778 --> 00:13:01,114
But you said you'd fire me first.

186
00:13:01,198 --> 00:13:03,742
Speaking of which, Special Forces, you…

187
00:13:03,825 --> 00:13:05,410
Please, sir!

188
00:13:06,495 --> 00:13:07,370
Please.

189
00:13:10,290 --> 00:13:11,500
…won't be fired.

190
00:13:14,085 --> 00:13:16,087
I think you misspoke just now.

191
00:13:17,088 --> 00:13:18,173
Not fired?

192
00:13:19,758 --> 00:13:21,343
Should I take it back then?

193
00:13:25,889 --> 00:13:29,059
Then please tell me what's going on.

194
00:13:29,142 --> 00:13:31,269
I said I wouldn't tell you that.

195
00:13:32,479 --> 00:13:35,649
I can't pretend I don't know
if I'm going to keep working for you.

196
00:13:36,191 --> 00:13:37,442
I need to stay prepared.

197
00:13:37,526 --> 00:13:38,610
Pretend you saw nothing.

198
00:13:39,778 --> 00:13:40,779
Or else,

199
00:13:41,905 --> 00:13:44,032
you'll resent me.

200
00:13:47,577 --> 00:13:49,287
Why are you keeping things from me?

201
00:13:52,165 --> 00:13:53,500
Do you not trust me?

202
00:13:57,504 --> 00:13:58,755
I'm warning you.

203
00:13:59,256 --> 00:14:01,007
Don't overstep your boundaries.

204
00:14:01,716 --> 00:14:03,301
You saving me from getting hit

205
00:14:03,385 --> 00:14:05,929
by a mere chandelier?

206
00:14:06,012 --> 00:14:10,433
You seem to think you've done
something extraordinary,

207
00:14:10,517 --> 00:14:13,812
but if you want to get paid,
just do what you're told.

208
00:14:53,184 --> 00:14:55,979
Gosh, what was that for? It's me.

209
00:14:59,274 --> 00:15:01,318
What the heck is this?

210
00:15:06,031 --> 00:15:06,906
Are you okay?

211
00:15:31,222 --> 00:15:32,474
I'm sorry.

212
00:15:32,557 --> 00:15:34,142
I didn't realize it was you.

213
00:15:38,897 --> 00:15:40,732
Seeing you apologize with that look

214
00:15:41,650 --> 00:15:42,942
is giving me butterflies.

215
00:15:43,943 --> 00:15:44,903
Was someone after you?

216
00:15:46,863 --> 00:15:48,031
What about your plans?

217
00:15:49,032 --> 00:15:50,867
I thought we were meeting tomorrow.

218
00:15:52,452 --> 00:15:53,578
I left something here.

219
00:15:56,206 --> 00:15:58,667
The tie you left behind
with an ulterior motive?

220
00:15:58,750 --> 00:16:00,669
You could tell?

221
00:16:03,963 --> 00:16:05,590
You're as perceptive as ever.

222
00:16:06,257 --> 00:16:08,051
Usually, women leave lipstick,

223
00:16:08,134 --> 00:16:10,595
wallets, compacts, and things in my car.

224
00:16:11,179 --> 00:16:14,557
But somehow, I didn't think you would.

225
00:16:15,892 --> 00:16:17,894
Did I make it too obvious?

226
00:16:19,646 --> 00:16:22,565
I still have a long way to go, don't I?

227
00:16:38,873 --> 00:16:39,999
You really want me to go?

228
00:16:40,083 --> 00:16:41,793
I don't like being the second option.

229
00:16:42,544 --> 00:16:45,004
I don't like men
who come and see me as a backup.

230
00:16:49,759 --> 00:16:52,262
If that's the case, you're no better.

231
00:16:52,345 --> 00:16:55,056
Weren't you more interested
in my plans than in me?

232
00:16:56,766 --> 00:16:58,977
"What went on in the Chairman's office?"

233
00:16:59,060 --> 00:17:01,896
"Is Managing Director Yoon
starting the succession process?"

234
00:17:02,772 --> 00:17:05,650
That's why you asked me to dinner, right?

235
00:17:07,569 --> 00:17:08,528
I'm leaving.

236
00:17:15,410 --> 00:17:18,455
Also, I didn't come here
because my plans fell through.

237
00:17:19,372 --> 00:17:20,623
I came because of you.

238
00:17:21,791 --> 00:17:24,294
So you can decide
whether we have dinner next time,

239
00:17:24,377 --> 00:17:25,962
Ms. Lee.

240
00:17:34,971 --> 00:17:36,347
It's been cut.

241
00:17:37,265 --> 00:17:41,019
Pliers, wire cutters, or bolt cutters
leave tool marks like this on the surface.

242
00:17:41,102 --> 00:17:42,645
It looks like someone cut it.

243
00:17:44,063 --> 00:17:45,523
Someone cut it?

244
00:17:46,357 --> 00:17:47,734
Who on earth would do this?

245
00:17:48,860 --> 00:17:50,153
Who were they trying to kill?

246
00:18:05,293 --> 00:18:09,047
You can push this by kicking it?

247
00:18:28,566 --> 00:18:29,859
Jeez.

248
00:18:40,578 --> 00:18:43,164
What are you doing here, Seok-jin?

249
00:18:43,957 --> 00:18:46,918
-Let's go. They're waiting.
-Did you come to pick me up?

250
00:18:47,585 --> 00:18:49,712
-I lost a game of rock paper scissors.
-I see.

251
00:18:49,796 --> 00:18:52,590
Is this the only umbrella?
There are extras at the station.

252
00:18:53,383 --> 00:18:54,342
I couldn't find any.

253
00:18:58,429 --> 00:19:01,724
I heard you barely dodged it.
Next time, protect yourself first.

254
00:19:01,808 --> 00:19:04,477
My body just reacted. I had to save him.

255
00:19:06,271 --> 00:19:07,146
Why?

256
00:19:07,939 --> 00:19:10,316
It's a suspect under investigation.
It's my job to--

257
00:19:10,400 --> 00:19:12,193
If you get hurt, none of this matters.

258
00:19:12,277 --> 00:19:14,946
Building rapport is important,
but don't get emotional.

259
00:19:16,072 --> 00:19:17,699
Yes, sir. I'll be careful.

260
00:19:24,455 --> 00:19:25,498
Is this it?

261
00:19:26,875 --> 00:19:28,585
Do you think I'll back off like this?

262
00:19:29,377 --> 00:19:31,880
I told you to stop clinging.

263
00:19:31,963 --> 00:19:33,882
Next time, it won't be just a warning.

264
00:19:36,426 --> 00:19:37,552
What do you mean by that?

265
00:19:48,062 --> 00:19:49,314
Do you smoke?

266
00:19:51,316 --> 00:19:52,233
You don't?

267
00:19:53,776 --> 00:19:55,820
Thanks to this,

268
00:19:57,697 --> 00:19:59,407
I recently saw something interesting.

269
00:20:11,794 --> 00:20:14,589
What if Yoon Yi-jun
didn't kill Secretary Han?

270
00:20:16,925 --> 00:20:18,343
Would I be in trouble?

271
00:20:23,556 --> 00:20:25,725
Isn't she Taekang's second daughter?

272
00:20:26,267 --> 00:20:27,894
Yes, Yoon Na-jung.

273
00:20:27,977 --> 00:20:31,481
Wait, that means the anonymous tip

274
00:20:31,564 --> 00:20:33,399
might be from Yoon Na-jung?

275
00:20:33,483 --> 00:20:37,236
-It's a possibility.
-No matter how awful someone is,

276
00:20:37,320 --> 00:20:40,239
they would still try to
protect their family.

277
00:20:40,740 --> 00:20:42,825
This Han Eun-young case…

278
00:20:43,326 --> 00:20:45,828
Why did the incident happen
just as Yoon Yi-jun started

279
00:20:45,912 --> 00:20:48,206
being mentioned in the press
as the next heir?

280
00:20:49,040 --> 00:20:51,876
Should we view this
as a family feud over succession?

281
00:20:53,169 --> 00:20:58,675
Yoon Na-jung is definitely the one
with the most to gain if he's the suspect.

282
00:21:03,972 --> 00:21:05,640
ARTICLE ONE: THE PARTY INVOLVED

283
00:21:05,723 --> 00:21:09,811
Our chairman sure loves his son.

284
00:21:17,276 --> 00:21:20,989
He's going to solidify the succession
in front of everyone, is that it?

285
00:21:21,823 --> 00:21:23,533
Is that also what you want,

286
00:21:24,993 --> 00:21:25,868
Ms. Yoon?

287
00:21:31,874 --> 00:21:33,251
Don't provoke me, Attorney Kim.

288
00:21:34,460 --> 00:21:35,795
When I lose my temper,

289
00:21:36,337 --> 00:21:38,256
even I can't control myself.

290
00:21:39,966 --> 00:21:43,594
I'm not sure. Even if Yoon Na-jung
had such intentions,

291
00:21:43,678 --> 00:21:45,221
all it did was add a witness.

292
00:21:45,304 --> 00:21:48,224
It doesn't prove Yoon Yi-jun's innocence.

293
00:21:49,308 --> 00:21:51,227
-This is difficult.
-That's the problem.

294
00:21:54,897 --> 00:21:56,065
Yes, Doctor.

295
00:21:58,026 --> 00:21:59,277
Thank you.

296
00:22:01,571 --> 00:22:04,282
It's the NFS report.
Detective Kang was right.

297
00:22:04,824 --> 00:22:07,201
A large amount of herbicide
was found in the milk.

298
00:22:07,285 --> 00:22:08,494
What?

299
00:22:09,037 --> 00:22:12,582
Why is this whole situation
getting so messy?

300
00:22:13,082 --> 00:22:15,334
The phone in the room
wasn't Han Eun-young's, right?

301
00:22:15,418 --> 00:22:17,211
It wasn't. I looked into the phone.

302
00:22:17,295 --> 00:22:20,089
It was distributed to
every Taekang employee three years ago.

303
00:22:20,590 --> 00:22:23,426
Yoon Yi-jun and Secretary Jung
also use the same model.

304
00:22:24,385 --> 00:22:26,721
Yoon Yi-jun is something else.

305
00:22:26,804 --> 00:22:29,348
Then why did he keep you out of that room?

306
00:22:29,432 --> 00:22:31,184
We got our hopes up for nothing.

307
00:22:31,809 --> 00:22:33,603
What does he use that room for?

308
00:22:36,564 --> 00:22:38,900
It was just…

309
00:22:40,693 --> 00:22:42,945
It was like a hobby room.

310
00:22:43,029 --> 00:22:46,282
You know,
everyone has a right to their privacy.

311
00:22:49,118 --> 00:22:51,537
-A billionaire's…
-Private life?

312
00:22:52,914 --> 00:22:54,373
His secret life?

313
00:23:45,508 --> 00:23:48,469
Good grief, all of you.

314
00:23:48,553 --> 00:23:50,638
What are you guys thinking about?

315
00:23:51,806 --> 00:23:53,474
There wasn't much.

316
00:23:53,558 --> 00:23:56,060
I got caught
because I was delayed retrieving this.

317
00:23:56,144 --> 00:23:57,145
Are you sure?

318
00:23:57,228 --> 00:23:59,981
You're not keeping the good stuff
for yourself, are you?

319
00:24:00,064 --> 00:24:02,608
You only get creative
when it comes to stuff like this.

320
00:24:02,692 --> 00:24:04,193
You really crossed the line there.

321
00:24:04,277 --> 00:24:05,611
That's ridiculous.

322
00:24:05,695 --> 00:24:07,613
Who cares if I cross the line,

323
00:24:07,697 --> 00:24:10,324
draw the line, erase the line,
or look at the line?

324
00:24:10,408 --> 00:24:12,577
I'm just using my own brain to imagine it.

325
00:24:12,660 --> 00:24:14,495
Don't overstep your boundaries.

326
00:24:14,579 --> 00:24:17,039
Pretend you saw nothing.

327
00:24:17,582 --> 00:24:19,709
Or else, you'll resent me.

328
00:24:23,921 --> 00:24:26,299
I told you to stop clinging.

329
00:24:26,382 --> 00:24:28,426
Next time, it won't be just a warning.

330
00:24:28,509 --> 00:24:30,553
-Hold on.
-I don't know.

331
00:24:31,179 --> 00:24:34,974
I don't know what I'll do to you
if you decide to take this further.

332
00:24:35,808 --> 00:24:37,435
This video…

333
00:24:37,518 --> 00:24:39,729
What if Yoon wasn't threatening
Han Eun-young?

334
00:24:39,812 --> 00:24:41,564
-What do you mean?
-What?

335
00:24:42,273 --> 00:24:45,610
What if he was trying to keep her out
of danger because of him?

336
00:24:45,693 --> 00:24:47,445
He said a similar thing to me.

337
00:24:47,528 --> 00:24:50,072
-Are you saying we should clear him?
-No.

338
00:24:50,156 --> 00:24:52,200
This is just a what-if.

339
00:24:53,034 --> 00:24:54,368
If we rule out Yoon Yi-jun,

340
00:24:54,452 --> 00:24:57,914
doesn't that connect the herbicide,
the chandelier,

341
00:24:57,997 --> 00:25:00,791
whoever is after Park Min-hwan,
and Yoon Na-jung?

342
00:25:00,875 --> 00:25:02,835
It makes sense.

343
00:25:03,628 --> 00:25:04,587
All right.

344
00:25:06,255 --> 00:25:08,549
When we hit a dead end,
we go back to the start.

345
00:25:08,633 --> 00:25:09,592
From now on,

346
00:25:10,301 --> 00:25:13,721
we need to consider the possibility
that Yoon Yi-jun isn't a suspect

347
00:25:13,804 --> 00:25:15,097
and start from square one.

348
00:25:15,181 --> 00:25:16,474
-Yes, sir.
-Yes, sir.

349
00:25:25,691 --> 00:25:27,151
-Hello?
-Were there more visitors?

350
00:25:27,235 --> 00:25:29,278
That's the full list of recent visitors.

351
00:25:29,362 --> 00:25:32,490
I checked everyone on the list,
and none of them are suspicious.

352
00:25:32,573 --> 00:25:34,033
None of them are suspicious?

353
00:25:35,493 --> 00:25:39,080
Choi Myeong-suk and Kim Si-hyun
are the only people who can freely visit.

354
00:25:40,122 --> 00:25:41,332
Noted for now.

355
00:25:46,170 --> 00:25:47,964
I'll help you, Ms. Choi.

356
00:25:48,047 --> 00:25:50,091
There's no need for that.

357
00:25:51,676 --> 00:25:52,635
Goodness.

358
00:25:53,302 --> 00:25:55,638
How are you so quick on your feet?

359
00:25:55,721 --> 00:25:59,642
Mr. Yoon would've been in big trouble
if it weren't for you.

360
00:26:01,018 --> 00:26:04,981
Why is Attorney Kim in charge of the milk
that Mr. Yoon drinks every now and then

361
00:26:05,731 --> 00:26:07,316
when he can't fall asleep?

362
00:26:07,400 --> 00:26:10,152
You're the one who manages his food.

363
00:26:10,236 --> 00:26:14,240
I think the milk is from Denmark or Italy.

364
00:26:14,740 --> 00:26:16,659
Anyway, it's imported organic milk.

365
00:26:16,742 --> 00:26:19,287
And there's an imported food shop
around his place.

366
00:26:21,414 --> 00:26:23,332
-I see.
-As for Attorney Kim,

367
00:26:23,416 --> 00:26:25,376
he comes by every few days.

368
00:26:25,459 --> 00:26:27,336
So he brings it when he can.

369
00:26:28,462 --> 00:26:30,548
It's good for me
since I have less work to do.

370
00:26:30,631 --> 00:26:33,092
That's why I don't even touch his milk.

371
00:26:38,014 --> 00:26:39,348
-I'll see you later.
-Okay.

372
00:26:43,436 --> 00:26:45,730
Kim Si-hyun and milk.

373
00:26:51,152 --> 00:26:52,570
Did you not sleep at all again?

374
00:26:53,362 --> 00:26:54,739
How many days has it been?

375
00:26:55,698 --> 00:26:57,408
It looks like you've slept well.

376
00:26:58,117 --> 00:26:59,577
Were you not worried about me?

377
00:27:02,455 --> 00:27:03,664
I was.

378
00:27:05,291 --> 00:27:06,500
You were?

379
00:27:07,376 --> 00:27:09,503
I thought you'd call, but you didn't.

380
00:27:10,087 --> 00:27:11,005
What?

381
00:27:11,088 --> 00:27:13,341
Let's change things up today.
Come on, stand up.

382
00:27:14,133 --> 00:27:15,217
Let's go.

383
00:27:18,387 --> 00:27:21,849
The quality of sleep is compromised
if you lack vitamin D.

384
00:27:21,932 --> 00:27:25,728
It's a scientific fact that it's good to
get sunlight at least three days a week.

385
00:27:25,811 --> 00:27:29,815
Especially for people like you,
who stay indoors all the time.

386
00:27:29,899 --> 00:27:31,734
I'm not indoors all the time.

387
00:27:31,817 --> 00:27:33,444
You don't need to exaggerate.

388
00:27:33,527 --> 00:27:35,529
I didn't. It's the truth.

389
00:27:35,613 --> 00:27:38,324
A reclusive loner with no social skills.

390
00:27:40,242 --> 00:27:43,245
Taekang employees usually
keep such thoughts to themselves.

391
00:27:43,329 --> 00:27:45,164
Why don't you try?

392
00:27:45,247 --> 00:27:48,959
Whatever. Can you just move a little more
when you're walking?

393
00:27:49,043 --> 00:27:53,089
You need to move more
when you have a lot on your mind.

394
00:27:53,172 --> 00:27:54,048
One, two.

395
00:27:54,131 --> 00:27:56,092
Don't treat me like some pet dog.

396
00:27:57,134 --> 00:27:59,678
I'll walk because I want to.

397
00:28:00,388 --> 00:28:02,890
Okay. Because you want to,

398
00:28:02,973 --> 00:28:05,309
you're going to run with me
in this direction.

399
00:28:05,851 --> 00:28:07,812
All right. One, three!

400
00:28:07,895 --> 00:28:09,271
I won't run.

401
00:28:09,355 --> 00:28:10,815
And you forgot to say two.

402
00:28:23,411 --> 00:28:26,372
But was I really in danger?

403
00:28:26,455 --> 00:28:29,375
It was quite a dangerous situation.

404
00:28:29,959 --> 00:28:31,627
That surprised me. Let's go.

405
00:28:41,720 --> 00:28:42,930
I have something to say.

406
00:28:43,013 --> 00:28:45,141
How are you tired already?

407
00:28:45,224 --> 00:28:46,058
Catch the ball!

408
00:28:51,605 --> 00:28:53,107
Thank you.

409
00:28:56,986 --> 00:28:58,404
Stop overdoing it and sit down.

410
00:29:02,408 --> 00:29:04,243
Why are you being overprotective?

411
00:29:06,454 --> 00:29:09,206
For the past few days,

412
00:29:09,290 --> 00:29:11,000
you've been strangely

413
00:29:13,794 --> 00:29:14,670
kind

414
00:29:16,213 --> 00:29:17,047
and caring.

415
00:29:17,798 --> 00:29:18,799
Have I?

416
00:29:19,341 --> 00:29:22,595
You used to look at me
with such hostility.

417
00:29:25,097 --> 00:29:27,141
Have you gone mad due to lack of sleep

418
00:29:27,224 --> 00:29:30,186
or because you haven't seen the sun
in so long?

419
00:29:31,729 --> 00:29:34,190
Do you realize how slow you were to react

420
00:29:34,273 --> 00:29:35,649
when the chandelier fell?

421
00:29:36,275 --> 00:29:39,570
If it weren't for me,
you'd be on a boat right now,

422
00:29:39,653 --> 00:29:41,989
crossing the River Styx.

423
00:29:42,072 --> 00:29:44,074
You told me not to cross boundaries.

424
00:29:44,158 --> 00:29:45,701
So what choice do I have?

425
00:29:45,784 --> 00:29:47,536
I need to be overprotective of you.

426
00:29:47,620 --> 00:29:49,121
I rescind your firing,

427
00:29:49,622 --> 00:29:51,999
and suddenly you've got some nerve.

428
00:29:55,211 --> 00:29:57,463
But you are correct.

429
00:30:00,132 --> 00:30:02,176
How did you become friends
with Kim Si-hyun?

430
00:30:04,220 --> 00:30:05,387
That was random.

431
00:30:07,973 --> 00:30:11,519
Is he currently your closest friend?

432
00:30:12,937 --> 00:30:14,688
Why would you

433
00:30:15,814 --> 00:30:19,026
suddenly be interested in Kim Si-hyun?

434
00:30:25,199 --> 00:30:28,494
The preparations for Mr. Yoon's succession
are nearly complete, sir.

435
00:30:34,625 --> 00:30:36,252
-Secretary Lee.
-Yes, sir.

436
00:30:38,879 --> 00:30:40,548
Make Yi-jun come to the meeting today.

437
00:30:40,631 --> 00:30:41,882
Yes, sir.

438
00:30:41,966 --> 00:30:44,260
I'll confirm again
through the secretary's office.

439
00:31:02,945 --> 00:31:05,489
Have you decided
whether to have dinner with me?

440
00:31:05,573 --> 00:31:07,366
I like having things clear.

441
00:31:07,908 --> 00:31:10,869
Whether it's dinner, where you stand,
or a relationship.

442
00:31:11,829 --> 00:31:13,956
-It's for your reference.
-How generous of you.

443
00:31:14,039 --> 00:31:16,709
A relationship with a man of the past?

444
00:31:16,792 --> 00:31:19,336
Whether we are exes or not

445
00:31:19,420 --> 00:31:20,838
is up to you, Attorney Kim.

446
00:31:23,882 --> 00:31:24,925
Up to me, you say?

447
00:31:34,101 --> 00:31:36,854
Are you giving this to Yoon Yi-jun today?

448
00:31:39,315 --> 00:31:41,900
Yes or no?

449
00:31:43,319 --> 00:31:46,030
Killed or didn't kill?

450
00:31:46,947 --> 00:31:49,575
All it takes is a statement from you
to resolve this issue.

451
00:31:49,658 --> 00:31:51,535
But I'd like to be of some help.

452
00:31:55,998 --> 00:31:58,459
There's Manager Park Min-hwan
in Accounting Team 3.

453
00:32:09,345 --> 00:32:12,598
He's the only witness
who saw who did what that day.

454
00:32:13,265 --> 00:32:15,934
But now he has disappeared.

455
00:32:17,227 --> 00:32:20,022
The issue is that he wasn't empty-handed.

456
00:32:21,774 --> 00:32:23,192
Aren't you curious

457
00:32:24,109 --> 00:32:26,737
what that son of yours
was doing behind your back?

458
00:32:29,073 --> 00:32:32,117
-Get to the point.
-He's not your only child.

459
00:32:33,035 --> 00:32:34,328
You should reconsider it.

460
00:32:42,836 --> 00:32:44,922
They say you have to participate.

461
00:32:45,005 --> 00:32:46,173
I am not going.

462
00:32:46,256 --> 00:32:47,466
I'll get in trouble.

463
00:32:47,549 --> 00:32:49,760
That's your problem. I'm not going.

464
00:32:49,843 --> 00:32:53,013
This is an order
from the chairman himself.

465
00:32:53,722 --> 00:32:56,058
My father never spoke to me about this.
I'm not going.

466
00:32:56,141 --> 00:32:58,268
Please, just this once.

467
00:32:58,352 --> 00:32:59,728
Just this once?

468
00:33:00,437 --> 00:33:03,607
I'll tell you one more time.
I'm not going.

469
00:33:03,691 --> 00:33:05,567
Seriously! Please!

470
00:33:05,651 --> 00:33:08,278
Get out! You're getting on my nerves.

471
00:33:08,362 --> 00:33:09,905
I saved you multiple times.

472
00:33:09,988 --> 00:33:11,990
And this is what I get!

473
00:33:14,410 --> 00:33:15,744
I shouldn't have saved him!

474
00:33:15,828 --> 00:33:18,080
I really shouldn't have.

475
00:33:27,756 --> 00:33:29,258
SECRETARY LEE HYE-JUNG

476
00:33:30,884 --> 00:33:33,554
Hello? This is Kang Jae-hee.

477
00:33:34,012 --> 00:33:36,724
Secretary Jung asked me to update you
on Mr. Yoon's attendance.

478
00:33:37,433 --> 00:33:38,600
Right.

479
00:33:39,101 --> 00:33:42,146
I don't think he'll be attending today.

480
00:33:42,229 --> 00:33:43,647
That's not good.

481
00:33:44,565 --> 00:33:48,277
The party won't be fun without its star.

482
00:33:51,405 --> 00:33:54,616
The day you gave me your card,
you told me to ask you anything.

483
00:33:55,117 --> 00:33:57,035
Right. Ask away.

484
00:33:57,119 --> 00:33:59,621
What's the reason Mr. Yoon has
to participate today?

485
00:33:59,705 --> 00:34:01,457
If things go as everyone expects,

486
00:34:01,540 --> 00:34:04,460
the chairman will name an heir.

487
00:34:05,711 --> 00:34:10,048
That means everyone else
will be there, right?

488
00:34:10,132 --> 00:34:11,425
Every last one of them.

489
00:34:13,427 --> 00:34:15,846
Every last one of them?

490
00:34:17,014 --> 00:34:18,015
I understand.

491
00:34:22,561 --> 00:34:23,479
Don't come in.

492
00:34:27,357 --> 00:34:28,984
Why did you bother to knock?

493
00:34:29,568 --> 00:34:31,445
Let's make a bet, sir.

494
00:34:31,528 --> 00:34:34,323
If you lose, you will go to that meeting.

495
00:34:34,406 --> 00:34:35,699
That won't be happening.

496
00:34:35,783 --> 00:34:38,202
Why would I make a bet with you?

497
00:34:38,285 --> 00:34:40,078
I won't do such a thing.

498
00:34:40,162 --> 00:34:41,955
But if you win,

499
00:34:42,790 --> 00:34:43,999
I won't report it.

500
00:34:44,082 --> 00:34:45,334
Won't report what?

501
00:34:45,417 --> 00:34:46,752
That the chandelier fell.

502
00:34:47,586 --> 00:34:49,880
I am obligated to make a report
as your secretary.

503
00:34:51,423 --> 00:34:53,383
I am your boss.

504
00:34:54,843 --> 00:34:56,970
I am part of Taekang's secretary team.

505
00:34:57,471 --> 00:35:02,142
I suppose the chairman will hear about it
through the chief secretary.

506
00:35:03,018 --> 00:35:04,102
Are you blackmailing me?

507
00:35:04,186 --> 00:35:05,395
I'm asking for cooperation.

508
00:35:05,479 --> 00:35:08,190
"There are mysterious things
going on around Mr. Yoon."

509
00:35:08,273 --> 00:35:11,360
"But he won't call the police
or call his family."

510
00:35:11,443 --> 00:35:12,945
"Because you'd be in a pickle

511
00:35:13,028 --> 00:35:16,114
if the chairman or anyone else
finds out about this."

512
00:35:16,198 --> 00:35:18,408
I warned you not to cross boundaries.

513
00:35:18,492 --> 00:35:21,495
The secretary's office
will hold me responsible if you don't go.

514
00:35:21,578 --> 00:35:23,580
Then I'll have no choice
but to tell the truth.

515
00:35:24,206 --> 00:35:28,085
Please decide
whether you want my cooperation or not.

516
00:35:32,422 --> 00:35:34,466
What's the bet?

517
00:35:39,429 --> 00:35:42,140
Picking a game where strength matters?
That's cheap.

518
00:35:42,224 --> 00:35:45,018
I chose it to keep things fair.
Want to switch?

519
00:35:45,102 --> 00:35:46,603
Boxing? Jujitsu? Pick your poison.

520
00:35:46,687 --> 00:35:49,439
Bad news for you.
I take herbal medicine, deer antler,

521
00:35:49,523 --> 00:35:51,024
and wild ginseng every year.

522
00:35:51,108 --> 00:35:53,819
Promise you'll go to the meeting
without a fight if I win.

523
00:35:53,902 --> 00:35:56,488
You better not mention
this meeting again if I win.

524
00:35:57,281 --> 00:35:59,157
You call this a man's hand?

525
00:35:59,241 --> 00:36:00,784
It looks way too delicate.

526
00:36:00,868 --> 00:36:01,869
How small your hand is.

527
00:36:01,952 --> 00:36:03,537
One would say this is a girl's hand.

528
00:36:03,620 --> 00:36:06,081
My hands are big.

529
00:36:10,544 --> 00:36:12,921
I'm at a disadvantage
the longer the arm wrestle lasts.

530
00:36:13,714 --> 00:36:15,090
Force is proportional to speed.

531
00:36:15,549 --> 00:36:18,343
Okay. The moment the game starts,
I'll finish him off with speed.

532
00:37:06,058 --> 00:37:07,976
Yes!

533
00:37:10,729 --> 00:37:12,981
That wasn't fair. You cheated!

534
00:37:13,065 --> 00:37:14,483
I learned from the best.

535
00:37:16,735 --> 00:37:17,861
I won.

536
00:37:21,031 --> 00:37:22,950
One more round. Best two out of three.

537
00:37:24,076 --> 00:37:26,536
You said it's one round.

538
00:37:26,620 --> 00:37:27,621
I'm busy, so goodbye.

539
00:37:28,455 --> 00:37:29,831
Where are you going?

540
00:37:31,083 --> 00:37:32,250
Get changed and come down.

541
00:37:34,795 --> 00:37:37,756
I'm not going!

542
00:37:39,633 --> 00:37:41,301
I'll see Yoon Na-jung

543
00:37:41,385 --> 00:37:44,596
and find out whether
she's just a witness or a suspect.

544
00:37:56,858 --> 00:37:59,403
It's my car. I choose where I want to sit.

545
00:38:07,661 --> 00:38:09,663
Even schoolchildren
are less childish than you.

546
00:38:10,080 --> 00:38:11,498
What was that just now?

547
00:38:27,973 --> 00:38:30,767
Everyone will be here on time, sir.

548
00:38:34,980 --> 00:38:36,773
If you're going to let him inherit it,

549
00:38:37,315 --> 00:38:40,193
why don't you name him heir
when things are quieter?

550
00:38:47,409 --> 00:38:50,579
We should make it quiet.
Time doesn't solve anything.

551
00:38:51,329 --> 00:38:52,664
I'm family too.

552
00:38:54,458 --> 00:38:55,834
I'm worried about my nephew.

553
00:38:57,377 --> 00:38:59,129
They say haste makes waste.

554
00:38:59,212 --> 00:39:02,883
We should settle things down first
before appointing him a successor.

555
00:39:02,966 --> 00:39:04,926
If he's not cut out for it,

556
00:39:05,886 --> 00:39:07,804
he shouldn't inherit it
in the first place.

557
00:39:07,888 --> 00:39:08,930
I see.

558
00:39:09,473 --> 00:39:11,391
Hand over management to him
and take it easy.

559
00:39:12,434 --> 00:39:15,520
I might step down too
and spend my days playing golf.

560
00:39:28,408 --> 00:39:29,493
Mom.

561
00:39:30,077 --> 00:39:31,286
Hey, Ka-on.

562
00:39:31,369 --> 00:39:33,663
Do I have to go?
I'm in my last year of high school.

563
00:39:34,206 --> 00:39:36,792
I don't have time to attend
my uncle's coronation.

564
00:39:36,875 --> 00:39:39,753
Sweetie, you're close to Uncle Yi-jun.

565
00:39:39,836 --> 00:39:41,880
That's the only reason I'm going.

566
00:39:42,589 --> 00:39:45,092
Who knows,
he might give me one of his subsidiaries.

567
00:39:45,592 --> 00:39:47,135
Is what I have not enough for you?

568
00:39:47,219 --> 00:39:49,054
Who do you take after to be this greedy?

569
00:39:49,137 --> 00:39:51,807
I'm still Chairman Yoon's granddaughter.

570
00:39:51,890 --> 00:39:53,433
You're the odd one, Mom.

571
00:40:40,564 --> 00:40:41,857
Is today finally the day?

572
00:40:41,940 --> 00:40:44,359
Probably, seeing as we were all called in.

573
00:40:44,442 --> 00:40:46,194
Then should we buy up some more shares?

574
00:40:46,278 --> 00:40:47,487
I should buy some too.

575
00:40:53,702 --> 00:40:56,037
You must be Yoon Yi-jun's
personal secretary.

576
00:41:01,168 --> 00:41:02,544
I was quite curious.

577
00:41:03,587 --> 00:41:07,716
I wonder what that picky Yoon Yi-jun
saw in you to hire you.

578
00:41:16,308 --> 00:41:18,435
We have plenty of time to find that out.

579
00:41:18,518 --> 00:41:20,353
Tell me how much you want.

580
00:41:22,772 --> 00:41:24,691
What can I do for you in return?

581
00:41:24,774 --> 00:41:26,818
They did tell me you were perceptive.

582
00:41:28,028 --> 00:41:30,447
What do you think
I'd want from my brother's secretary?

583
00:41:30,530 --> 00:41:32,324
I want his information.

584
00:41:33,533 --> 00:41:35,577
That attitude,
like this isn't her first time…

585
00:41:37,037 --> 00:41:40,457
She approached Yoon Yi-jun's confidants
the same way in the past.

586
00:41:42,125 --> 00:41:45,295
I have someone to congratulate,
so excuse me.

587
00:41:46,129 --> 00:41:49,007
I'll look forward to hearing
how much that intel is worth.

588
00:41:50,634 --> 00:41:51,676
You wouldn't need to,

589
00:41:53,303 --> 00:41:54,512
because it won't happen.

590
00:42:04,397 --> 00:42:05,899
How many people

591
00:42:06,816 --> 00:42:10,111
did you approach to bribe them like this?

592
00:42:11,321 --> 00:42:13,615
Did you do the same thing
to Secretary Han?

593
00:42:15,784 --> 00:42:17,202
I thought you were clever.

594
00:42:19,496 --> 00:42:20,455
Hey.

595
00:42:21,539 --> 00:42:23,124
For guys like you,

596
00:42:23,208 --> 00:42:25,126
everything depends on
which side you stand.

597
00:42:27,003 --> 00:42:28,713
You'd better stand on the right side.

598
00:42:28,797 --> 00:42:30,048
Which side I am on

599
00:42:31,258 --> 00:42:33,426
is none of your business.

600
00:42:38,014 --> 00:42:40,308
Yi-jun, I heard you were on sick leave.

601
00:42:40,392 --> 00:42:42,727
I'm going to Fiji soon. Join me.

602
00:42:42,811 --> 00:42:44,938
Why don't we get some fresh air together?

603
00:42:46,356 --> 00:42:48,483
Unfortunately, I'm not that unwell.

604
00:42:51,820 --> 00:42:54,948
I know I haven't been my best,
so thank you for inviting me.

605
00:43:01,705 --> 00:43:02,872
You're here, Na-jung.

606
00:43:04,666 --> 00:43:06,251
You're here too, Chief Secretary?

607
00:43:09,254 --> 00:43:12,590
Right. It's no place for someone like me.

608
00:43:13,425 --> 00:43:15,593
Of course you should join us, Uncle.

609
00:43:15,677 --> 00:43:18,096
Especially on a joyful day like this.

610
00:43:19,889 --> 00:43:23,226
Retail's operating profit
is way up year-over-year.

611
00:43:24,978 --> 00:43:27,439
It's been smooth sailing
since CEO Yoon took over, right?

612
00:43:28,982 --> 00:43:30,317
You were always second place.

613
00:43:31,151 --> 00:43:33,194
You barely won once.

614
00:43:33,695 --> 00:43:35,613
Aren't you ashamed to compliment yourself?

615
00:43:38,533 --> 00:43:39,701
I'll try harder.

616
00:43:40,201 --> 00:43:42,704
I try hard, but I'm always lacking.

617
00:43:42,787 --> 00:43:46,207
But Yi-jun, whom you trust the most,
is different.

618
00:43:47,625 --> 00:43:50,086
He led the TF team this far,
though it was difficult.

619
00:43:50,170 --> 00:43:52,422
From here on out, he'll soar.

620
00:44:00,638 --> 00:44:02,599
-Take it out.
-Yes, sir.

621
00:44:23,912 --> 00:44:25,830
SELLER: YOON TAE-SIK, BUYER: YOON YI-JUN

622
00:44:53,733 --> 00:44:56,194
TAEKANG RETAIL
STOCK PURCHASE AGREEMENT

623
00:45:05,328 --> 00:45:06,663
I said not to cause trouble.

624
00:45:07,539 --> 00:45:10,834
If you can't even keep that one promise,
how do you expect to run a company?

625
00:45:15,755 --> 00:45:17,173
I'll hand the company

626
00:45:17,257 --> 00:45:20,510
to whoever can keep Taekang's dominance
across all its affiliates.

627
00:45:20,593 --> 00:45:21,636
So…

628
00:45:26,349 --> 00:45:27,976
all of you, bring your results.

629
00:45:29,561 --> 00:45:31,020
I'll name an heir

630
00:45:32,230 --> 00:45:34,149
at the next shareholder meeting.

631
00:45:41,489 --> 00:45:42,449
Let's eat.

632
00:45:51,082 --> 00:45:52,083
Congratulations.

633
00:45:53,334 --> 00:45:54,919
Take this chance to get some rest.

634
00:46:03,720 --> 00:46:05,096
So what happened?

635
00:46:06,806 --> 00:46:08,057
That's why

636
00:46:09,058 --> 00:46:10,894
you should've behaved.

637
00:46:10,977 --> 00:46:12,812
You can't even take what's served to you.

638
00:46:14,189 --> 00:46:16,941
I can't tell whether the chalice
holds poison or fine wine.

639
00:46:18,860 --> 00:46:19,861
What choice do I have?

640
00:46:20,445 --> 00:46:22,739
I'll have to drink it myself.

641
00:46:22,822 --> 00:46:26,159
You think you drank poison, don't you?

642
00:46:31,664 --> 00:46:34,250
That's why I told you to choose well.

643
00:46:36,878 --> 00:46:38,880
Your master has lost his power,

644
00:46:40,590 --> 00:46:42,467
and you failed to read the situation.

645
00:47:02,445 --> 00:47:03,780
Do you need consolation?

646
00:47:06,741 --> 00:47:09,702
I'm not that good at doing it,

647
00:47:09,786 --> 00:47:10,787
but I can try.

648
00:47:12,830 --> 00:47:16,709
They say we all get an equal share
of happiness and misfortune.

649
00:47:17,252 --> 00:47:20,296
Since you've had one misfortune today,

650
00:47:20,380 --> 00:47:22,632
you've got one happiness left.

651
00:47:22,715 --> 00:47:24,801
Just be quiet and drive.

652
00:47:26,094 --> 00:47:28,596
-Yes, sir.
-I expected this.

653
00:47:30,348 --> 00:47:32,809
I didn't go there

654
00:47:32,892 --> 00:47:36,145
just because I lost some stupid bet.

655
00:47:36,229 --> 00:47:39,107
So you expected that this would happen?

656
00:47:40,650 --> 00:47:43,987
I thought you were in this for the money,
not out of loyalty.

657
00:47:50,493 --> 00:47:51,327
Are you okay?

658
00:47:54,455 --> 00:47:55,498
I'm sorry.

659
00:47:55,957 --> 00:47:57,834
I just reacted in case you got hurt.

660
00:48:00,503 --> 00:48:01,838
In case I got hurt?

661
00:48:01,921 --> 00:48:04,299
I'm being overprotective
according to someone I know.

662
00:48:05,508 --> 00:48:09,220
Who else would be on your side if not me?

663
00:48:12,599 --> 00:48:15,476
Who said I let you be on my side?

664
00:48:27,155 --> 00:48:29,699
LEGAL TEAM ATTORNEY KIM SI-HYUN

665
00:48:32,160 --> 00:48:34,579
Weren't you more interested
in my plans than in me?

666
00:48:35,204 --> 00:48:37,957
That's why you asked me to dinner, right?

667
00:48:39,500 --> 00:48:41,628
I didn't come here
because my plans fell through.

668
00:48:42,045 --> 00:48:43,171
I came because of you.

669
00:48:44,297 --> 00:48:46,299
SAESUPGIL HAEJANGGUK

670
00:48:49,844 --> 00:48:51,804
SECRETARY LEE HYE-JUNG

671
00:48:58,770 --> 00:49:01,522
The number you've dialed is unavailable.

672
00:49:01,606 --> 00:49:03,274
You'll be connected to voicemail…

673
00:49:13,993 --> 00:49:16,162
I've confirmed
the security system is working,

674
00:49:16,245 --> 00:49:17,455
so I'll be heading home.

675
00:49:18,081 --> 00:49:19,332
Do you want a drink?

676
00:49:19,916 --> 00:49:21,751
No, thank you. I'll get going.

677
00:49:22,377 --> 00:49:23,378
Okay, then.

678
00:49:35,765 --> 00:49:38,476
I'm going to claim overtime pay for today,
and I can't drink.

679
00:49:38,559 --> 00:49:41,062
But I'm a good listener.

680
00:49:42,230 --> 00:49:43,064
You can't drink?

681
00:49:43,856 --> 00:49:45,400
You are banned from drinking.

682
00:49:45,483 --> 00:49:48,945
The moment your drinking habits come out,
this operation is done for good.

683
00:49:49,028 --> 00:49:50,071
Remember that.

684
00:49:51,739 --> 00:49:52,740
I can't, sir.

685
00:49:52,824 --> 00:49:55,993
If you can, just drink one glass with me.

686
00:49:59,080 --> 00:50:01,457
-Okay, but--
-But what?

687
00:50:03,459 --> 00:50:05,795
Why do you always have so many rules?

688
00:50:06,421 --> 00:50:08,256
Can't you just do it?

689
00:50:09,424 --> 00:50:13,344
Let's play a game of truth while we drink.

690
00:50:13,928 --> 00:50:17,640
You have to answer one question properly.

691
00:50:34,365 --> 00:50:35,658
Do you know, Attorney Kim?

692
00:50:36,409 --> 00:50:37,452
Dogs

693
00:50:38,995 --> 00:50:40,621
can't choose their masters.

694
00:50:41,998 --> 00:50:43,624
The master chooses their dogs.

695
00:50:45,793 --> 00:50:48,963
I think it's time
you make it clear who your master is.

696
00:50:57,054 --> 00:50:58,055
First of all,

697
00:50:59,140 --> 00:51:00,183
I'm not a dog.

698
00:51:01,225 --> 00:51:02,852
But if you must know,

699
00:51:03,936 --> 00:51:05,021
I serve Taekang.

700
00:51:05,688 --> 00:51:07,315
What if I take control of Taekang?

701
00:51:11,986 --> 00:51:13,404
The question must've been hard.

702
00:51:14,655 --> 00:51:15,948
Let's make this easy.

703
00:51:17,158 --> 00:51:19,243
Where is Manager Park Min-hwan?

704
00:51:25,917 --> 00:51:27,543
That's the most humiliating thing

705
00:51:28,461 --> 00:51:30,254
I've heard all year.

706
00:51:30,338 --> 00:51:32,673
Come on, I've already seen everything.

707
00:51:32,757 --> 00:51:35,551
There's no need to make excuses.

708
00:51:35,635 --> 00:51:37,762
It's fine. Come here.

709
00:51:37,845 --> 00:51:39,680
I respect your personal preference.

710
00:51:41,057 --> 00:51:42,183
Goodness.

711
00:51:48,356 --> 00:51:50,733
Fine. Tell me.

712
00:51:52,068 --> 00:51:53,110
What did you say?

713
00:51:53,986 --> 00:51:55,321
Can I say it again?

714
00:51:55,404 --> 00:51:56,614
You better.

715
00:52:00,827 --> 00:52:02,537
It's a little lousy.

716
00:52:03,079 --> 00:52:04,789
-Lousy?
-Lousy!

717
00:52:04,872 --> 00:52:08,584
Why do you only collect stuff like that?

718
00:52:12,630 --> 00:52:14,674
Pervert. Geek.

719
00:52:14,757 --> 00:52:17,301
Pervert? Geek?

720
00:52:19,345 --> 00:52:20,805
You're crazy.

721
00:52:20,888 --> 00:52:22,014
That's so funny.

722
00:52:23,140 --> 00:52:24,559
-Follow me.
-No!

723
00:52:25,226 --> 00:52:26,394
Hey!

724
00:52:27,061 --> 00:52:28,062
Just kidding.

725
00:52:31,315 --> 00:52:34,235
You want me to follow you?
I saw everything already.

726
00:52:39,156 --> 00:52:42,660
If you kindly open the door
for me like this,

727
00:52:43,286 --> 00:52:44,120
I guess I'll look.

728
00:52:50,459 --> 00:52:53,462
I didn't know
you could turn the lights on.

729
00:52:57,091 --> 00:52:59,510
My gosh, what's all this?

730
00:53:12,732 --> 00:53:15,943
Do they really need to
flaunt their bodies…

731
00:53:16,027 --> 00:53:17,028
ARA, THE SEA GODDESS

732
00:53:17,111 --> 00:53:19,113
…while fighting villains
and upholding justice?

733
00:53:19,989 --> 00:53:25,494
If that's the main reason
you collect them,

734
00:53:26,078 --> 00:53:28,706
then you're definitely a perverted geek.

735
00:53:29,290 --> 00:53:30,124
Cut that out.

736
00:53:32,752 --> 00:53:33,753
That scared me.

737
00:53:34,503 --> 00:53:37,381
I was so surprised
when I saw this last time.

738
00:53:38,299 --> 00:53:40,509
Why did they make it so big?

739
00:53:41,552 --> 00:53:44,221
But I also like her.

740
00:53:45,765 --> 00:53:46,724
Ara.

741
00:53:51,812 --> 00:53:53,898
-This is a collection of Ara?
-Wait.

742
00:53:54,857 --> 00:53:55,858
Don't touch it.

743
00:53:58,694 --> 00:54:00,613
-Fine, I won't.
-Come here.

744
00:54:00,696 --> 00:54:01,906
-Fine.
-Here.

745
00:54:01,989 --> 00:54:04,533
Okay. Let's have the second round.

746
00:54:07,328 --> 00:54:10,081
My type is a strong woman who can fight.

747
00:54:10,623 --> 00:54:12,833
How dare you call me a pervert

748
00:54:15,127 --> 00:54:16,295
and a geek?

749
00:54:19,173 --> 00:54:22,927
Is that really something
I deserve to be insulted for?

750
00:54:25,805 --> 00:54:29,850
It's not like I'm swearing at you
or anything.

751
00:54:31,352 --> 00:54:32,311
You.

752
00:54:33,312 --> 00:54:37,775
You insulted not only me,
but also all the women who are my type.

753
00:54:38,359 --> 00:54:40,611
-Apologize.
-Okay.

754
00:54:42,446 --> 00:54:44,615
I'm very sorry.

755
00:54:47,201 --> 00:54:48,035
Happy?

756
00:54:49,578 --> 00:54:51,914
But now that I am here again,

757
00:54:52,415 --> 00:54:54,041
I can see that it's colorful.

758
00:54:55,042 --> 00:54:57,378
It's nice. It's like a heroine museum.

759
00:54:59,588 --> 00:55:01,966
You told me not to touch that one.

760
00:55:03,467 --> 00:55:04,719
Is that your favorite?

761
00:55:05,886 --> 00:55:07,054
It is.

762
00:55:08,347 --> 00:55:11,934
That is the last gift I got from my mom.

763
00:55:13,602 --> 00:55:14,520
Yi-jun.

764
00:55:15,229 --> 00:55:18,691
Ara will always protect you.

765
00:55:18,774 --> 00:55:20,192
-Okay?
-Okay.

766
00:55:21,027 --> 00:55:22,028
It's for you.

767
00:55:26,407 --> 00:55:28,951
I made it myself. Do you like it?

768
00:55:29,035 --> 00:55:30,036
Yes.

769
00:55:37,710 --> 00:55:42,131
But why do you only have heroines?

770
00:55:46,802 --> 00:55:48,804
Was your childhood dream to be a hero?

771
00:55:49,680 --> 00:55:50,765
That's adorable.

772
00:55:52,266 --> 00:55:53,559
I wanted to protect them.

773
00:55:55,352 --> 00:55:57,521
But I couldn't protect anyone.

774
00:55:59,356 --> 00:56:01,650
So I ended up collecting these.

775
00:56:02,193 --> 00:56:03,319
Right.

776
00:56:03,819 --> 00:56:07,531
After all, you're not as cool as them.

777
00:56:08,616 --> 00:56:12,286
I think the biggest issue is
that personality of yours.

778
00:56:13,037 --> 00:56:14,955
Your personality makes me want a drink.

779
00:56:16,624 --> 00:56:18,250
Is drunken honesty your thing?

780
00:56:19,085 --> 00:56:20,127
But in a way,

781
00:56:21,253 --> 00:56:23,172
you are similar to the heroines.

782
00:56:25,216 --> 00:56:28,469
Having the determination
to protect someone.

783
00:56:29,095 --> 00:56:31,097
It's not an easy thing.

784
00:56:32,389 --> 00:56:35,476
It takes courage. "Courage."

785
00:56:36,727 --> 00:56:38,104
What's the use?

786
00:56:38,854 --> 00:56:40,815
I couldn't protect anyone anyway.

787
00:56:42,066 --> 00:56:43,067
What?

788
00:56:48,155 --> 00:56:50,199
You protected me.

789
00:56:54,620 --> 00:56:58,290
You were deliberately cruel

790
00:56:58,374 --> 00:57:00,543
so I wouldn't find anything out

791
00:57:00,626 --> 00:57:02,711
and put myself in danger,

792
00:57:04,880 --> 00:57:05,714
right?

793
00:57:08,717 --> 00:57:10,553
You probably did the same
to Secretary Han.

794
00:57:12,054 --> 00:57:16,058
I know everything you said
at the columbarium

795
00:57:17,268 --> 00:57:18,519
was out of guilt.

796
00:57:24,150 --> 00:57:26,735
What do you know?
Don't talk like you know everything.

797
00:57:28,779 --> 00:57:30,823
You just let me think

798
00:57:31,407 --> 00:57:33,742
that you were a crappy boss.

799
00:57:34,326 --> 00:57:36,162
Even I can tell after knowing you briefly.

800
00:57:36,245 --> 00:57:39,248
Don't you think Secretary Han
and your mother knew?

801
00:57:41,876 --> 00:57:44,253
They must have understood it all.

802
00:57:50,259 --> 00:57:52,595
Why are you crossing the boundaries again?

803
00:57:54,471 --> 00:57:55,514
Why do you keep

804
00:57:57,641 --> 00:58:00,060
seeing things I don't want you to see?

805
00:58:08,319 --> 00:58:09,695
I won't ask you anything else

806
00:58:12,156 --> 00:58:13,490
for the game of truth.

807
00:58:16,327 --> 00:58:19,663
You have to answer the question, okay?

808
00:58:24,877 --> 00:58:26,378
You didn't do it,

809
00:58:28,756 --> 00:58:29,590
did you?

810
00:58:37,389 --> 00:58:38,515
You didn't kill

811
00:58:40,476 --> 00:58:41,685
Secretary Han, did you?

812
00:58:53,489 --> 00:58:54,490
I didn't.

813
00:59:00,204 --> 00:59:01,413
That's all I need.

814
00:59:07,836 --> 00:59:08,837
Special Forces.

815
00:59:11,173 --> 00:59:12,007
Are you okay?

816
00:59:15,261 --> 00:59:16,679
Did you really just fall asleep?

817
00:59:20,724 --> 00:59:21,767
Special Forces.

818
00:59:23,519 --> 00:59:25,688
Can you get up for a second?

819
00:59:26,188 --> 00:59:27,273
Okay.

820
00:59:30,943 --> 00:59:31,986
My gosh!

821
00:59:34,822 --> 00:59:35,906
What the heck?

822
00:59:38,117 --> 00:59:39,285
Come over here!

823
00:59:40,786 --> 00:59:42,413
You evil cat.

824
00:59:48,085 --> 00:59:49,628
You're just like Yoon Yi-jun!

825
01:00:08,605 --> 01:00:09,857
You little brat!

826
01:00:15,362 --> 01:00:17,323
Come over here.

827
01:00:17,406 --> 01:00:20,034
You stupid cat!

828
01:00:24,580 --> 01:00:26,081
That little cat

829
01:00:26,790 --> 01:00:30,127
is making me exercise at this hour.

830
01:00:31,003 --> 01:00:32,004
Where are you?

831
01:00:41,221 --> 01:00:43,640
You! You're busted.

832
01:00:44,641 --> 01:00:46,101
I'm Kang Jae-hee.

833
01:00:46,935 --> 01:00:50,189
There's no one I can't catch
if I put my mind to it.

834
01:00:51,607 --> 01:00:53,108
Try me.

835
01:00:53,901 --> 01:00:55,235
Come on. Glare at me.

836
01:00:56,487 --> 01:00:57,613
Here I come.

837
01:00:58,113 --> 01:01:00,366
One, two…

838
01:01:04,870 --> 01:01:05,746
Three!

839
01:01:07,081 --> 01:01:08,123
What?

840
01:01:08,749 --> 01:01:11,335
-Stop.
-What's going on?

841
01:01:12,586 --> 01:01:13,587
Damn it.

842
01:01:14,380 --> 01:01:16,006
What's this?

843
01:01:17,007 --> 01:01:18,133
Who the heck are…

844
01:01:27,309 --> 01:01:28,352
Are you living

845
01:01:29,103 --> 01:01:30,354
like there's no tomorrow?

846
01:01:30,437 --> 01:01:32,106
You better behave.

847
01:01:35,109 --> 01:01:37,277
Who hits someone

848
01:01:39,154 --> 01:01:40,823
and just walks off?

849
01:01:46,578 --> 01:01:48,247
Special Forces! You!

850
01:01:49,164 --> 01:01:50,207
You have the right

851
01:01:50,290 --> 01:01:52,626
to remain silent

852
01:01:53,168 --> 01:01:54,002
and the right to…

853
01:01:54,795 --> 01:01:57,214
-Wait. Where are the handcuffs?
-Move!

854
01:01:59,508 --> 01:02:00,634
Move!

855
01:02:03,429 --> 01:02:05,180
-I'm dizzy.
-Special Forces, you little…

856
01:02:14,356 --> 01:02:15,232
Come here!

857
01:03:52,538 --> 01:03:53,830
SPECIAL THANKS TO
KIM DO-YOON AND JUNG YOO-MIN

858
01:03:53,914 --> 01:03:55,374
The real killer is someone else.

859
01:03:55,457 --> 01:03:57,918
-They're clearly targeting Yoon Yi-jun.
-Yoon Yi-jun's fiancée is coming to Korea.

860
01:03:58,001 --> 01:04:00,462
A silver spoon whose dad
is a leading presidential candidate.

861
01:04:00,546 --> 01:04:02,089
-Did you two sleep together?
-No.

862
01:04:02,172 --> 01:04:03,006
Are you crazy?

863
01:04:03,090 --> 01:04:06,218
I was just upset over
my secretary's mistake.

864
01:04:06,301 --> 01:04:07,344
This much?

865
01:04:07,427 --> 01:04:08,512
How cute.

866
01:04:08,595 --> 01:04:09,763
We need to find it first.

867
01:04:09,846 --> 01:04:11,515
Bring Park Min-hwan to me,

868
01:04:11,598 --> 01:04:13,517
and I'll tell you what you want to know.

869
01:04:13,600 --> 01:04:16,144
I have to do everything I can
to prevent further harm.

870
01:04:16,228 --> 01:04:18,230
-Is he in a safe place?
-Yoon Na-jung?

871
01:04:18,897 --> 01:04:21,650
I need to check something with you.

872
01:04:21,775 --> 01:04:24,778
Translated by Leo Chung
